# midiout, midiround, midithru, midilocal, midiburst, midioutlat (since M6b;
#   R-MIDIOUT-1 to R-MIDIOUT-8): MIDI out, captured with --midi-out (fwtest
#   0.5.0), scripts written by tools/midi_scripts.py; the MIDI out record at
#   0x01c00734. midiout: what the panel sends (golden midi-out.csv and .txt).
#   midiround: midiout's golden capture played into MIDI in; the engine ends
#   as midiout's did. midithru: the thru test build (thru on, out on channel
#   2) with MIDI in and the panel at once (golden). midilocal: local control
#   off by CC 122, then on again (screen at 700 ms, golden). midiburst: a
#   test build that queues more than the queue holds in one block (golden).
#   midioutlat: 20 keys, key down to the note on's first byte on the wire.
#   Since M8a these three start from a flash chip whose settings say
#   "Knobs: direct" (out/fw/knobs-direct.flash.bin, tools/fw-suite.py), so
#   KNOB1 to KNOB4 are M5's controls, as they were written for.
#   midiout's golden capture (golden-midi/midiout/) and midiround's script
#   move together: tools/regolden.py --write runs tools/midi_scripts.py
#   when it writes midiout's capture again; a change of midiout's
#   messages is made by hand, then tools/midi_scripts.py, in the same
#   commit.
